---
name: nearby_affordances
description: >
  The perception half of the affordance layer (#446 decision 2, issue #613):
  a one-line hint naming visible-but-distant arenas and the affordance tags
  they carry, appended to a live decide observation so a brain can choose to
  travel toward one. Offers themselves stay in-scope only (npc.tools_for), so
  this line NEVER widens the toolset -- it only motivates the walk. Rendered by
  cognition.nearby_affordances_line() and appended only on the real-brain tool
  path, so the deterministic mock (and the byte-identical bake) never read it.
  The arena list is assembled in Python (it is data); only the wording lives
  here.
inputs:
  arenas:
    type: string
    description: >
      Pre-joined "<name> (<tags>)" fragments, e.g.
      "Van Pelt — Moelis Reading Room (studyable); Houston Hall (dining)".
sample:
  arenas: "Van Pelt — Moelis Reading Room (studyable); Houston Hall (dining)"
---
Nearby, worth traveling to: {{ arenas }}.
